  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`IMutableTeventDispatcher` and `ITeventSubscriber` are safe to use from several threads at once:** to dispatch, to register handlers and to dispose subscribers. Before, two dispatches on different threads could corrupt the dispatcher's cache of the handlers each tevent type routes to (\"Operations that change non-concurrent collections must have exclusive access\"), and a registration or disposal racing a dispatch could corrupt its lists of subscriptions. Handlers still run synchronously on the dispatching thread, outside the dispatcher's lock; each dispatch calls the handlers subscribed when it began. A dispatch of a tevent whose type the dispatcher has already resolved takes no lock at all, and is as fast as before.\n- `IMutableTeventDispatcher.Handles` no longer lets a later `Dispatch` of a tevent nothing handles pass silently: asking about such a tevent cached an empty list of handlers for its type, and the dispatch then skipped the `TeventUnhandledException` check.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Internals.SystemCE 0.7.0-internal (was 0.4.0-internal), Compze.Threading 0.11.0-alpha (was 0.9.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
